{"title":"Career Roadmap · Medical Record Officer","role":"Medical Record Officer","summary":"A Medical Record Officer (MRO) manages the creation, organization, accuracy, storage, retrieval and controlled use of patient health records.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Medical Records & Health Information"},"about":[{"label":"Important","text":"Medical Record Officer is a health-information and hospital-administration role rather than a direct clinical-treatment role. Job titles and eligibility can vary between hospitals and government/private recruitment systems. Strong knowledge of medical terminology, health information management, coding, data quality, confidentiality and hospital information systems is particularly valuable."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Medical Record Officer (MRO) manages the creation, organization, accuracy, storage, retrieval and controlled use of patient health records."},{"type":"h","text":"The role sits at the intersection of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Healthcare"},{"text":"Medical documentation"},{"text":"Health information management"},{"text":"Hospital administration"},{"text":"Data quality"},{"text":"Medical coding"},{"text":"Privacy and confidentiality"},{"text":"Digital health systems"},{"text":"Statistics and reporting"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A modern Medical Record Officer increasingly works with Electronic Health Records (EHR), Hospital Information Systems (HIS), dashboards, coding systems, data-quality processes and digital records rather than only paper files."},{"type":"h","text":"Career Flow"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical Records / Health Information Education"},{"type":"h","text":"Hospital Records Internship"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical Records Trainee"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical Record Officer"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Medical Record Officer"},{"type":"h","text":"Hea